  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nit's like 'disabled' is being used to indicate 'useless' (or, more gently, 'off') and it's rude. i am not useless because i have a disability! (i mean the politics of the word 'disability', you know? but lets not go there). the button is not disabled. the button is not useless. the button is being used to prevent further action without fulfilling some previous requirement. what the button _is_ is unclickable. The internet does amazing things for people with disabilities. So it's 2025 and _why_ does using a button make me feel like i'm coding with people who don't get it? I _know_ y'all get it. I know you're all about it. So could we get something done about it?\n\nlol not mad at yall, its just been a long friday (it is almost sunday)\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\n'disabled'\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nlike, im not saying get rid of 'disabled' as a prop. im just begging y'all to allow the option to use 'unclickable' instead.\n\n### Anything else?\n\num, let me know if i can help? i've never done this before. i'll try to check in with this for awhile.\n\nAlso posted this to https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/issues/32654#issue-3484331945.",
